  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "> Mainly an escape hatch until vLLM pins an AITER release with the fix.\r\n\r\nI would push the AITER side fix and wait for that. In the meanwhile you can use `VLLM_ROCM_QUICK_REDUCE_QUANTIZATION=INT6` that still routes to HIP QR.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-03T07:45:22Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64929#issuecomment-6598195569",
      "id": 6598195569,
      "updated_at": "2026-11-03T07:45:22Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "mjkvaak-amd"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks @mjkvaak-amd, agreed. The AITER side fix is ROCm/aiter#7258 (approved). I've moved this back to draft and will close it once that lands in the AITER version vLLM pins.\n\nIf you hit wrong outputs with INT4 QuickReduce on ROCm in the meantime (e.g. MiniMax-M3 MMMU around 0.3): either wait for the AITER fix, or set `VLLM_ROCM_QUICK_REDUCE_QUANTIZATION=INT6`, which still routes to vLLM's HIP QuickReduce.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:29:03Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64929#issuecomment-6614687168",
      "id": 6614687168,
      "updated_at": "2026-11-03T20:29:03Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "vorapolsiloai"
      }
    }
  ],
